Support XMG APEX 16 MAX (M25), board X6DR5xxK (Uniwill/Tongfang, board vendor NB02).

1. Let the drivers load on this non-TUXEDO-branded board (tuxedo_compatibility_check
   otherwise refuses: DMI vendor is SchenkerTechnologiesGmbH and the Ryzen 9 8945HX
   is not in the legacy CPU skip list).
2. Exclude the board from "universal fan control": the EC advertises the feature
   (0x078e bit 6) and accepts the 0x07c5/0x07c6/0x0fxx custom tables, but ignores
   them. The legacy full-fan-mode path (0x0751 bit 0x40 + 0x1804/0x1809) works.
   Newer tuxedo-drivers have the same exception for sibling boards (X6FR5xxY etc.).

Applies to tuxedo-drivers v4.20.1.

--- a/src/tuxedo_compatibility_check/tuxedo_compatibility_check.c
+++ b/src/tuxedo_compatibility_check/tuxedo_compatibility_check.c
@@ -215,6 +215,12 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id tuxedo_dmi_string_match[] = {
 			DMI_MATCH(DMI_CHASSIS_VENDOR, "TUXEDO"),
 		},
 	},
+	{
+		// XMG APEX 16 MAX (M25), Schenker Technologies, Uniwill/Tongfang barebone
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "X6DR5xxK"),
+		},
+	},
 	{ }
 };
 
--- a/src/uniwill_keyboard.h
+++ b/src/uniwill_keyboard.h
@@ -1522,6 +1522,12 @@
 		return 0;
 	}
 
+	// XMG APEX 16 MAX (M25): the EC claims universal fan control but ignores the
+	// custom fan tables; the legacy full-fan-mode path works.
+	if (dmi_match(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "X6DR5xxK")) {
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	ret = uniwill_read_ec_ram(0x078e, &data);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		return ret;
